# The bookseller's trade (docs/systems/dialogue.md, "Types"): what any dealer
# in books offers, whoever he is: asked for a title, and selling a book. The
# librarian of the candle lane is one. {name} is whoever speaks.
# Every text is the user's to write; each beat's intent: says what it must do.

== character bookseller
colour: ink
voice: male
intent: a dealer in old and rare books: knows his stock to the shelf, haggles, and never hurries

== beat open
intent: a nameless bookseller looks up from his ledger at a customer: civil, measuring what the customer can pay
{name}: <<A bookseller looks up from his ledger.>>
>> <<Ask him for a title.>> -> ask_title
>> [if purse>=3] <<Buy a book from him.>> -> buy_book
> <<Leave.>> -> end

== beat ask_title
intent: the trade's answer to "have you got...": what he keeps, what he will not sell, and how long a search would take
{name}: <<He says what he keeps, what he will not sell, and how long a search would take.>>
-> end

== beat buy_book
do: charge(3), give(bought_book)
intent: he sells an ordinary volume off his shelves (3 coins), wrapped in brown paper; one remark about it as he hands it over
{name} [nod]: <<He wraps a book in brown paper and takes his coin.>>
-> end

== item bought_book
name: <<a book bought off the shelves>>
look: book
intent: an ordinary book any bookseller sells: not the curandera's book; what is it?
